<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Allies of World War II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Allies, Allied powers, United Nations</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, formally referred to as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> from 1942, were the international military coalition formed during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">World War II</a> (1939–1945) to oppose the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis powers</a>; its principal members were the United Kingdom, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. When the war broke out on 1 September 1939 the coalition consisted of the United Kingdom, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> with their dependencies. The Soviet Union joined after the German invasion of June 1941 and the United States after the attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a> in December 1941. The Declaration by United Nations of 1 January 1942, signed by 26 countries, formalised the alliance, which became the basis of the modern United Nations.</p></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> of 1919 established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> in an attempt to create a system of collective security. Its covenant obliged members to protect the political and territorial integrity of all members against aggression, and four major allies of the First World War, the United Kingdom, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, became permanent members of its council. The League was weakened by the failure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to join and by cumbersome rules for enforcing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">History</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> on 1 September 1939, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> declared war on 3 September. Most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> was automatically at war, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> declared war separately; Canada was the last, on 10 September. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> forces invaded northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> added the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, and many governments of occupied countries went into exile.</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, which had cooperated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in the partition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, joined after the German invasion of June 1941. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> had supplied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> through the destroyers-for-bases deal of September 1940 and the Lend-Lease programme from March 1941, and declared war after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>. Winston Churchill called the association the Grand Alliance. At the First Washington Conference Franklin D. Roosevelt proposed the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>, and the Declaration by United Nations of 1 January 1942 was signed by 26 countries. Conferences at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casablanca">Casablanca</a>, Washington and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> in 1943 shaped strategy: the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, and the postponement of a landing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> until May 1944.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> peace treaties of 1947 distinguished Associated Powers from former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> states that had become co-belligerents. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, which armistice terms of 3 September 1943 had taken out of the Axis, declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in October 1943. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> changed sides after King Michael deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ion-antonescu">Ion Antonescu</a> on 23 August 1944, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> declared war on Germany on 8 September 1944. After the war the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and the Declaration that bound them became the basis of the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>. The wartime alliance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the United Kingdom broke down and evolved into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Allies of World War II” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>When the Comintern was dissolved in 1943 so that the Soviet Union could keep its alliance with the other <b>Allies of World War II</b>, a new anthem was needed to replace &quot;The Internationale&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/state-anthem-of-the-soviet-union">State Anthem of the Soviet Union</a></li></ul></section>
